here were still some  loose ends  Loki being one of them so Loki was most  likely the only if not one of the only  major threats to the T a V and other  alternate realities now it is worth  noting that in the comics the TIV isn't  particularly good at their job in fact  they fail to stop a nihilist and Kang  the Conqueror in the comics and they  actually have to call on help from the  Avengers quite often but somehow they  managed to capture Loki unless Loki  wanted to be caught let's go back to the  very first Avengers film where Nick Fury  captures Loki but  very quickly points out that he feels  like loki is the only one that actually  wants to be on the ship which was true  loki intentionally got caught which  leads me to believe that now he  intentionally got caught by the t AV  they were probably following him around  for some time and knowing loki it was  probably pretty annoying to him  and we hear him say in the trailer i'm  going to burn this place to the ground  and he says that with that classic loki  mischievous smile and that smile  definitely looks like he's saying this  was my plan get captured so you could  bring me to your base and so i could  escape and burn it down but who knows  perhaps they're competent in the MCU and  actually did manage to capture loki but  let me know what you think about the  first looks that we got at the falcon in  the Winter Soldier series and the Loki  series as well be sure to let me know  your thoughts in the comments down below  and don't forget to like the video and  subscribe when notifications turned on  so you can stay up to date on everything  relating to the MCU and so you can enter  my giveaway for a chance to win an Xbox  one or a ps4 the winner gets to choose  and I'm picking a winner at five hundred  and fifty thousand subscribers don't  forget to follow me on Instagram and  Twitter and as always thank you all so  much for watching  woof woof


